        "prior_assessment": "Estonia's defense posture has undergone a major strategic reorientation, redirecting \u20ac500 million from traditional heavy armor to modern asymmetric capabilities including air defense and drone warfare, while establishing forward military infrastructure directly on the Russian border at Narva, representing the most significant procurement and positioning shift since the defense industrial expansion began.",
        "updated_assessment": "The strategic reorientation documented last week (\u20ac500M procurement shift, Narva base) remains the dominant security posture fact, but two this-week developments add important qualifications. First, KAPO's 2025 annual report reveals the active hybrid threat environment has expanded in scope: record Russian agent detentions (16), growing Chinese influence operations targeting Estonian public figures, and Eastern Orthodox Church clergy permit revocations as active countermeasures all confirm the intelligence-security domain is under intensifying multi-vector pressure. Second, US delivery delays for HIMARS ammunition \u2014 directly relevant to last week's asymmetric capability build-up \u2014 create an operational gap in the procurement reorientation. Former EDF commander Herem suggests up to 2\u20133 years of delay is manageable, with South Korean Hanwha contracts as backup, but the gap is real and documented. The net assessment: Estonia's posture intent remains unchanged, but its execution faces a supply chain constraint that the defence ministry is publicly managing while seeking alternative sourcing. The competing interpretation on KAPO: the record arrest numbers may reflect improved detection capability rather than a surge in Russian recruitment efforts \u2014 KAPO is getting better at finding what has always been there.",
